From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sat, 27 Jun 2026 11:09:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 04470/11362] [outer-loop] Verifier-gated-reasoning #1-risk
 DE-RISKED POSITIVE (no-retrieval model-native verifier discriminates
 hallucinations)

De-risk for the arXiv:2603.09906 verifier-gated-reasoning line: can a Carnot-side,
no-retrieval, model-native signal discriminate Qwen3.5-9B's correct vs hallucinated
factual answers? (the #1 risk in the SOTA-ingestion note.)

Hardened run (n=500, 45 correct / 455 hallucinated, SimpleQA-Verified, GPU 1):
  self_consistency AUROC 0.759, paired-bootstrap CI95 [0.698, 0.818] (lower > 0.5),
  label-shuffle control 0.536. answer_logprob 0.657, p_true 0.657 also above chance.
  => RESOLVED POSITIVE: no retrieval grounding needed for the discrimination step.

Prelim n=120 artifact preserved (only 10 correct = underpowered; superseded by the
hardened n>=30 + CI95-lower>0.5 gate). Residual carried into the full experiment:
this measured the FINAL answer; the A/B/C experiment gates on INTERMEDIATE facts and
on headroom (C>B). Note's risk #1 section updated to record the resolution.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
